{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790012626,"nonce":"D1UaRXq5cNl99Ni4ssvYA4OP5G8=","title":"dev:spawn-pawn --age gives children an adult body type and missing clothing textures","message":"dev:spawn-pawn generates the pawn at the kind's own age and only then overwrites ageTracker.AgeBiologicalTicks (DevVerbs.SpawnPawn). Body type and apparel are chosen during generation for the ORIGINAL age, so a pawn forced to a child age keeps an adult body type.\n\n**Seen twice on 2026-09-21 (languages test runs):**\n- Tribal_Child --age 7: warning \"Kip had body type set to  as a child.\", red_error \"Failed to find any textures at Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/TribalA/TribalA_Child\", and the pawn drawn as the red missing-texture X.\n- Colonist --age 10: the same warning, plus red_error for ShirtBasic_Child.\n\n**Fix:** pass the age into the request (PawnGenerationRequest fixedBiologicalAge, plus fixedChronologicalAge no lower than it) instead of setting it after generation, so life stage, body type and apparel are generated for that age.\n\n**Acceptance**\n\n1. dev:spawn-pawn --kind Tribal_Child --age 7 and --kind Colonist --age 10: no body-type warning, no red_error, a child body type.\n2. An adult --age 30 is unchanged.","files":null}]}